# Email project

## Scope

`email/frontend`, `email/backend`, `email/backend/migrations` — standalone transactional email microservice.

## Ports and env

| Layer | Port | Env file |
|-------|------|----------|
| Frontend | 3014 | `email/frontend/.env` |
| Backend | 4014 | `email/backend/.env` |

`JWT_SECRET` must match Identity backend. `EMAIL_SERVICE_API_KEY` shared with Identity and WebOnOne backends for internal send API.

## Ownership

- Templates, queue, SMTP, send history, providers, branding — own DB `webonone_email`.
- JWT verification locally on public routes; session role from JWT `platform_role` / `company_id` claims (no local role table).

## Platform shell — mirror Identity profile

Email must follow the **same three-layer pattern** as Identity profile. See [platform-shell-navigation.mdc](platform-shell-navigation.mdc).

| Role | Profile (reference) | Email (this service) |
|------|---------------------|----------------------|
| Inbound layout | `identity/.../app/AppLayout.tsx` | `email/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx` |
| Inbound home + bootstrap | `identity/.../profile/pages/ProfilePage.tsx` | `email/frontend/src/features/dashboard/pages/DashboardPage.tsx` |
| Bootstrap util | `bootstrapProfileSession.ts` | `features/auth/utils/bootstrapPlatformSession.ts` |
| Return URL util | `profileReturn.ts` | `features/auth/utils/platformReturn.ts` |
| Outbound profile | — | `features/auth/utils/redirectToIdentityProfile.ts` |
| Core nav | `shell/config/navItems.ts` | `shell/config/coreNavItems.ts` + `shell/utils/buildAppNav.ts` |

Consumers (WebOnOne, Identity): `handleEmailClick` in `AppLayout` + `redirectToEmail.ts` — **no** `/go/email` route or redirect page.

**Satellite → Data peer nav:** `VITE_DATA_ORIGIN`, `features/data/utils/dataConfig.ts`, `redirectToData.ts`, `shell/utils/externalNavActions.ts` — see [platform-shell-navigation.mdc](platform-shell-navigation.mdc) satellite peer nav.

**Unified loading overlay:** `features/auth/context/PlatformLoadingContext.tsx`, `app/LazyRoute.tsx`, single overlay in `app/AppLayout.tsx` — [loading-empty-states.mdc](loading-empty-states.mdc).

## Core-hosted form dialogs

When Email is embedded in WebOnOne, form dialogs (e.g. templates) must use the **peer-dialog** bridge — host `CustomDialog` header/footer + `/embed/dialogs/…` body — not an iframe-local `CustomDialog`. Recipe: [platform-shell-navigation.mdc](platform-shell-navigation.mdc); sizing/footer rules: [dialog-windows.mdc](dialog-windows.mdc).

Reference: `email/frontend/src/features/templates/components/TemplateFormDialog.tsx`.

## UI Kit

All interactive UI must use `@webonone/ui-kit` — see [ui-kit-consumption.mdc](ui-kit-consumption.mdc). Do not duplicate UI Kit primitives.

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w email-root
npm run migrate -w email-root
```

Cross-service flow requires Identity + WebOnOne running for full platform nav test.
